      "detail": "Attempts against workloads whose dataset licence does not permit publishing derived results are withheld: their rows, groups and fixture records are absent. The release spec names the workloads and the reason.",
      "id": "workloads-withheld"
    },
    {
      "affects": "every row",
      "detail": "This release combines several diagnostic campaigns run between 2026-08-26 and 2026-09-03 while the harness, the replay server and Swath were evolving. Every attempt pins its exact tool, image, platform, fixture and replay identities, but rows from different groups are not comparable merely because they share a release; the report's asymmetry table names the cases that matter.",
      "id": "multi-campaign-corpus"
    },
    {
      "affects": "every row with replay != null",
      "detail": "Replay applies one fixed deadline per request shape, taken from the median of the Swath capture run and checked against a serial client on the same bucket. It has no tail, no throttling and no rise under load, and it prices a request by its syntax. The serial checks are internal controls recorded in working notes, not published receipts. docs/instrument.md carries the model, its provenance and its known skews.",
      "id": "latency-model-is-not-s3"
    },
    {
      "affects": "every row with replay != null",
      "detail": "The replay server's fixture and the subject's output live on the same boot disk of one VM. CPU sets are separated by physical core; disk bandwidth, page cache and memory bandwidth are not, and no disk metric is exported.",
      "id": "shared-host-disk"
    },
    {
      "affects": "REPORT.md",
      "detail": "Some statements in REPORT.md rest on the private run summary, the runner log or the tool's source rather than on a field of these rows (the listing-phase time inside a live-S3 run, a diagnosis of why a run was slow, a Spot preemption). The report labels each such statement with its source; none is a release field.",
      "id": "prose-cites-private-evidence"
    },
    {
      "affects": "every row with fixture != null",
      "detail": "Fixtures are published as digests and shape metrics only. The fixture bytes and the original evidence store are private, and the source buckets are mutable, so the identical replay experiment cannot be rerun from this repository alone; the release is auditable, not independently reproducible.",
      "id": "fixtures-not-published"
    },
    {
      "affects": "every row with version ending in -SNAPSHOT",
      "detail": "Rows whose Swath version is 0.2.5-SNAPSHOT (2026-08) or 0.3.2-SNAPSHOT (2026-09-03) ran unreleased builds pinned by image digest: the 0.3.2-SNAPSHOT rows are the sink-channel fix (upstream #209, commit cc052c9) and its lane-routing follow-up (#210, commit 5cdaeaf, not merged) measured on sentinel-cogs before v0.3.2 was cut. They are diagnostics of a change, not release rows; the released-build rows of the same shapes are the s032-* groups.",
      "id": "unreleased-swath-builds"
    },
    {
      "affects": "every row with replay == null",
      "detail": "Live-S3 rows launched in parallel from the same project and VPC (2026-09-02 four buckets; 2026-09-03 the s032-s3-* groups) share the path out of the VPC. The sentinel-cogs 32-vCPU TSV row of 2026-09-03 listed 23 % slower while four other live-S3 jobs ran than the same build did alone earlier that morning, with S3 first-byte latency and sink waits both higher; the 64-vCPU row reproduced its solo figure within 2 %. Where a solo re-run exists it is the row to cite; the report names them.",
      "id": "concurrent-live-s3-launches"
    },
    {
      "affects": "s4cmd",
      "detail": "s4cmd is a roster subject with no attempt in this release: it lists through the legacy ListObjects v1 API, which the replay server does not serve, and it requires credentials on live S3.",
      "id": "roster-subject-not-run"
    }
  ],
